From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:17:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: say why the cmd/frame interlock let a frame
 through

dsi-collide fired twice during a brightness ramp on a kernel with
cmd_frame_serialize=Y, which the protocol says cannot happen: a kickoff takes
cmd_mutex before CTL_START, a transfer holds cmd_mutex across the DMA, and a
transfer that starts while a frame is pending waits for CMD_MDP_DONE. Both
CTL_START paths route through dpu_encoder_kickoff(), so on paper there is no
window.

Reading the code further only produces more theories, so make the detector
report the state that would distinguish them. Exactly one of these has to be
false when it fires:

  sync=0    cmd_sync_host was not this host, so msm_dsi_cmd_kickoff_begin()
            and the frame_pending wait BOTH silently no-op
  pend=1    a frame was pending and we transmitted anyway
  waited=2  the 100 ms wait timed out and we transmitted anyway
  waited=0  the wait was skipped entirely

Diagnostic only; no behaviour change.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index 068f2b69e10b..b12579824d4a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -176,6 +176,8 @@ struct msm_dsi_host {
 	 */
 	wait_queue_head_t frame_wait;
 	bool frame_pending;
+	/* diagnostic: 0 = wait skipped, 1 = waited and frame cleared, 2 = timed out */
+	u8 collide_waited;
 	u32 mdp_done_cnt;
 
 	u32 err_work_state;
@@ -1611,9 +1613,25 @@ static int dsi_cmd_dma_tx(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host, int len)
 	if (!(msm_host->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO)) {
 		u32 status = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_STATUS0);
 
+		/*
+		 * When this fires the interlock let a frame through, so print
+		 * why. Measured 2026-08-21: it fired twice on a brightness
+		 * ramp with cmd_frame_serialize=Y, which the protocol says is
+		 * impossible -- kickoff takes cmd_mutex (held here) and the
+		 * transfer waits on frame_pending. Exactly one of these must
+		 * be false: sync=0 means cmd_sync_host was not this host, so
+		 * BOTH sides silently no-op; pend=1 means the wait was skipped
+		 * or timed out; waited=1 with pend=1 means it timed out and we
+		 * transmitted anyway.
+		 */
 		if (status & DSI_STATUS0_CMD_MODE_MDP_BUSY)
-			pr_warn("dsi-collide: frame started during cmd DMA, status=%08x ret=%d\n",
-				status, ret);
+			pr_warn("dsi-collide: frame started during cmd DMA, status=%08x ret=%d sync=%d ser=%d pend=%d waited=%d mdp_done=%u\n",
+				status, ret,
+				READ_ONCE(cmd_sync_host) == msm_host,
+				cmd_frame_serialize,
+				READ_ONCE(msm_host->frame_pending),
+				msm_host->collide_waited,
+				msm_host->mdp_done_cnt);
 	}
 
 	return ret;
@@ -1915,10 +1933,12 @@ static ssize_t dsi_host_transfer(struct mipi_dsi_host *host,
 	 * controller (CMD_MDP_DONE). The reverse direction is covered by
 	 * msm_dsi_cmd_kickoff_begin() taking cmd_mutex, which we now hold.
 	 */
+	msm_host->collide_waited = 0;
 	if (cmd_frame_serialize && READ_ONCE(cmd_sync_host) == msm_host) {
 		long rc = wait_event_timeout(msm_host->frame_wait,
 					!READ_ONCE(msm_host->frame_pending),
 					msecs_to_jiffies(100));
+		msm_host->collide_waited = rc ? 1 : 2;	/* 2 = timed out */
 		if (!rc)
 			pr_warn("dsi-framewait: frame_pending stuck (mdp_done irqs=%u)\n",
 				msm_host->mdp_done_cnt);
